<summary>Review details</summary>

### Suppressed comments (1)

**include/xrpl/tx/paths/detail/StrandFlow.h:823**
* The comment says this branch is handling a FillOrKill offer, but this code path also triggers when `offerCrossing == OfferCrossing::No` (regular payment flow) and when `offerCrossing == Yes` (non-sell crossing). Reword to describe the actual condition: partial payments are disabled, so any shortfall is an error; for offer crossing this enforces FillOrKill for non-`tfSell`.
```
        if (!partialPayment)
        {
            // If we're offerCrossing a !partialPayment, then we're handling a FillOrKill.
            if (offerCrossing != OfferCrossing::Sell)
            {
                return {tecPATH_PARTIAL, actualIn, actualOut, std::move(ofrsToRmOnFail)};
            }
```

